H261 — the SELECT command in prompts/ok-1.md §6 against the queue's own parser
rows=347  rows containing an escaped pipe=44

A · CLOSED rows the old command OFFERS as work: 13
     H82    queue=DONE
     H18    queue=DONE
     H27    queue=DONE
     H36    queue=DONE
     H40    queue=DONE
     H53    queue=DONE
     H67    queue=DONE
     H72    queue=DONE
     H84    queue=DONE
     H168   queue=DONE
     H199   queue=DONE
     H218   queue=DONE
     H254   queue=DONE

B · OPEN rows the old command HIDES: 4
     H2     queue=OPEN
     H17    queue=OPEN
     H29    queue=OPEN
     H41    queue=OPEN

Both directions are real and the second is the one I did not predict:
a row whose ITEM text contains the word DONE lands in field 4 after the
naive split, so the command reads the item as a status and drops the row.
